---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import {
  PRODUCT_NAME,
  CURRENT_LINE,
  V1_LINE,
  V2_LINE,
  VENDOR,
  COMPANY_KVK,
} from '../data/product-facts.mjs';

// OWNER: set the effective date at GA (mirrors the terms page).
const PRODUCT = `${PRODUCT_NAME} ${CURRENT_LINE}`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — mod_pagespeed"
  description="Cookieless analytics — no tracking cookies. How modpagespeed.com handles personal data, and what the software you run does and does not send."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-text-body">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-text-annotation">
      Effective date: September 2026 &middot; Version 2026-09
    </p>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-text-muted">
      This notice covers how the <strong>modpagespeed.com</strong> website and its services process personal
      data, and what the software you install does with data. {VENDOR} operates several websites; this
      page is the specific notice for modpagespeed.com. For the company-wide policy, see the
      <a
        href="https://we-amp.com/privacy/"
        class="text-interactive hover:text-interactive-hover underline"
        >We-Amp B.V. privacy policy</a
      >, of which this is a part.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 space-y-10">
      <!-- Controller -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Who is responsible</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          The data controller is {VENDOR}, a company registered in the Netherlands.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-none text-text-muted space-y-1">
          <li>{VENDOR}, Castricum, the Netherlands</li>
          <li>KvK (Chamber of Commerce): <span class="font-mono">{COMPANY_KVK}</span></li>
          <li>VAT (BTW): <span class="font-mono">NL852784429B01</span></li>
          <li>
            Privacy contact:
            <a
              href="mailto:privacy@we-amp.com"
              class="text-interactive hover:text-interactive-hover underline">privacy@we-amp.com</a
            >
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- The software -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">The software you run</h2>
        {
          /* TODO(counsel-T5): the predecessor-line sentence below is drafted from the relicensing
            decision's retirement sequence: installs sold a production license may keep polling the
            retired license-renewal endpoints, which first go inert and are decommissioned only
            after every legacy paid term expires; the hosted collection machinery was removed.
            Counsel to confirm the final wording against engineering facts — exactly which
            predecessor releases, in which license state, can still contact the retired endpoints.
            Minimal alignment only; the rest of this notice is untouched. */
        }
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          {PRODUCT} runs on your servers. It sends no telemetry to us and opens no outbound connection
          of its own accord. The only traffic that leaves a host is what you, the operator, configure:
          fetches to your own origin for the resources it optimizes and, when you enable browser analysis,
          requests to the pages you point it at (and whatever those pages load). Your visitors&rsquo;
          data never reaches {VENDOR}, and we have no way to see it. This is true with or without a
          support subscription.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          The predecessor lines &mdash; mod_pagespeed {V1_LINE} and ModPageSpeed {V2_LINE} &mdash; behave
          the same way for installs that run without a paid license: they never sent us anything. Installs
          of predecessor releases sold a production license may still contact our retired license-renewal
          endpoints; those endpoints no longer record anything and are being switched off as the last
          legacy terms expire.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          Because of this, for most deployments {VENDOR} is not a processor of your visitors&rsquo; data
          at all. Where we do act as a processor for a business customer &mdash; for example during a
          support engagement in which you share logs or configuration with us &mdash; a Data Processing
          Agreement is available on request at
          <a
            href="mailto:privacy@we-amp.com"
            class="text-interactive hover:text-interactive-hover underline">privacy@we-amp.com</a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- What we process -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">What the website processes, and why</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          We keep data collection to the minimum each service needs. The activities below cover
          everything modpagespeed.com does with personal data.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-6 space-y-6">
          <!-- Analytics -->
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-text-body">Website analytics</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
              We use a self-hosted Umami instance (umami.we-amp.com) to count page views and see
              which pages are useful. Umami is cookieless and does not build a profile across sites.
              It records aggregate signals such as page path, referrer, approximate region, browser
              and device type, plus a few named interactions on this site (for example, clicks on a
              download button). We do not use this data to identify individuals.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-annotation">
              Lawful basis: legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR) in measuring and improving the
              site, balanced against the low-impact, cookieless design.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Server logs and GeoIP -->
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-text-body">Server logs and IP geolocation</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
              Like any web server, ours keeps standard access logs: the connecting IP address, the
              request line, a timestamp, the referrer and the user agent. The server also looks up
              the connecting IP address in two DB-IP Lite databases held on the server itself
              (country, and autonomous-system number), refreshed monthly. The lookup happens on our
              server; the address is not sent to DB-IP or to any other third party for this. We use
              the country to show prices in your region where the site displays them, and to limit
              the administrative interface of our self-hosted analytics to addresses in the
              Netherlands (no visitor-facing effect). We use the network number to leave visits from
              datacenter and cloud-provider networks out of the site analytics; such visits are
              simply not counted, and an address that cannot be resolved is never dropped.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-annotation">
              Lawful basis: legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR) in operating and securing the
              site and in keeping its analytics meaningful.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- PSI proxy -->
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-text-body">PageSpeed Insights proxy (/analyze)</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
              When you submit a URL on the
              <a href="/analyze/" class="text-interactive hover:text-interactive-hover underline"
                >/analyze</a
              > page, our server forwards that URL to Google&rsquo;s PageSpeed Insights API (operated
              by Google in the United States) and returns the result. The URL you submit may itself contain
              personal data if you choose to enter such a URL &mdash; please don&rsquo;t. We also log
              and rate-limit by your IP address to prevent abuse of the shared API access.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-annotation">
              Lawful basis: legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR) in offering the tool and
              protecting it from abuse. Use of Google&rsquo;s API is also subject to Google&rsquo;s
              own terms and privacy policy.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- RenderPeek -->
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-text-body">AI-readability scanner (RenderPeek)</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
              The AI-readability scanner renders a URL you submit so we can report how it looks to
              automated agents. Rendering runs on Google Cloud Run. As with the PageSpeed Insights
              proxy, we process the submitted URL and your IP address for the request and to
              rate-limit abuse. We do not retain the rendered page content beyond what is needed to
              return your result.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-annotation">
              Lawful basis: legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR) in offering the tool and
              protecting it from abuse.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Subscriptions -->
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-text-body">Subscriptions</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
              When you take out a support subscription or a hardened-builds subscription, we process
              your name, email address, organization and order details to provide the subscription,
              to give you access to the subscriber repository, and to invoice. Where a merchant of
              record handles the payment (currently FastSpring), it is the seller of record and an
              independent data controller for the billing, payment and tax data it collects under
              its own privacy policy; we receive the order and subscription record.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-annotation">
              Lawful basis: performance of a contract (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR) and our legal obligations
              for bookkeeping and tax (Art. 6(1)(c) GDPR).
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Contact -->
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-text-body">When you contact us</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
              If you email us or use the contact form, we process the message and your contact
              details to reply and keep a record of the correspondence. When you submit the contact
              form, your name, email address, chosen topic and message are posted to a We-Amp
              contact-handling endpoint, which delivers the message to us (as a Telegram
              notification) and logs it so we can follow up. If that submission fails, or if
              JavaScript is disabled, the form falls back to opening a pre-filled email in your own
              mail client instead.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-annotation">
              Lawful basis: legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR) in responding to your request,
              or steps toward a contract (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR) where relevant.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Marketing / product updates -->
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-text-body">Marketing and product updates</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
              Where a form on this site offers it &mdash; the newsletter signup in the footer and at
              the foot of blog posts, or asking for a full RenderPeek report &mdash; you can opt in
              to receive product and web-performance updates by email. Opting in is always a
              separate, un-ticked choice. While we set up a dedicated email tool, we record your
              address and consent through the same contact-handling endpoint described above. We
              only send these updates to people who have opted in; every message will include an
              unsubscribe link; and we do not sell or share your address with third parties for
              their own marketing.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-annotation">
              Lawful basis: consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR). You can withdraw consent at any time by
              emailing
              <a
                href="mailto:privacy@we-amp.com"
                class="text-interactive hover:text-interactive-hover underline"
                >privacy@we-amp.com</a
              > (and, once we start sending updates, via the unsubscribe link in any message).
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Retention -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">How long we keep data</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          We retain personal data no longer than necessary for the purpose it was collected.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc list-inside text-text-muted space-y-1">
          <li>
            <strong>Analytics:</strong> aggregate event data is retained on a rolling basis and is not
            tied to an identified person.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Server access logs (including PageSpeed Insights / scanner requests):</strong>
            access and rate-limit logs are kept short-term for abuse prevention and operations, then rotated
            out.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Subscriptions, orders and invoices:</strong> retained for as long as your subscription
            is active and afterward as required by Dutch tax law (a 7-year retention obligation applies
            to accounting records).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Correspondence:</strong> kept as long as needed to handle your request and for a reasonable
            period afterward.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Newsletter / marketing consent:</strong> your email address and consent record are
            kept for as long as you remain subscribed. While we set up a dedicated email tool, these are
            held in the interim server-side log described above; once that tool is live we migrate your
            record to it and remove the interim copy.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- Sub-processors -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Sub-processors</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          We rely on a small number of third parties to run modpagespeed.com. Each processes data
          only as needed for its function.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-sm text-text-muted">
            <thead class="text-text-body">
              <tr class="border-b border-border">
                <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold">Provider</th>
                <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold">Purpose</th>
                <th class="py-2 font-semibold">Location</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="border-b border-border">
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">Google (PageSpeed Insights API)</td>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">Scores URLs submitted to /analyze</td>
                <td class="py-2">United States</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-border">
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">Google Cloud (Cloud Run)</td>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4"
                  >Hosts the AI-readability scanner that renders submitted URLs</td
                >
                <td class="py-2">United States (us-central1)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-border">
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">DB-IP</td>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">
                  GeoIP databases (IP-to-Country Lite and IP-to-ASN Lite) held on our own server for
                  regional price display and analytics filtering; no data is sent to DB-IP
                </td>
                <td class="py-2">N/A (local lookup)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">Telegram (Telegram FZ-LLC)</td>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">
                  Delivers contact-form and newsletter-signup messages to us as a notification (the
                  message also resides in our server-side log, which is the durable record)
                </td>
                <td class="py-2">Outside the EU/EEA</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-text-annotation">
          Payments for subscriptions are handled by a merchant of record (FastSpring) as an
          independent data controller &mdash; not a processor acting on our behalf &mdash; so it is
          described under &ldquo;Subscriptions&rdquo; above rather than listed here. We self-host
          our analytics (Umami) on our own infrastructure, so analytics is not handled by a
          third-party processor.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-text-annotation">
          GeoIP data is provided by <a
            href="https://db-ip.com"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-interactive hover:text-interactive-hover underline">DB-IP.com</a
          > under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- International transfers -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">International transfers</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          Some of the third parties we work with are based outside the EU/EEA &mdash; in the United
          States (FastSpring and Google) and elsewhere (Telegram, which relays contact-form and
          newsletter-signup notifications). Where personal data is transferred outside the EU/EEA,
          we rely on appropriate safeguards such as the EU Standard Contractual Clauses and, where
          applicable, the providers&rsquo; certification under the EU&ndash;U.S. Data Privacy
          Framework.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Rights -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Your rights</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          Under the GDPR you have the right to access, rectify, erase, restrict or object to the
          processing of your personal data, and the right to data portability. To exercise any of
          these, email
          <a
            href="mailto:privacy@we-amp.com"
            class="text-interactive hover:text-interactive-hover underline">privacy@we-amp.com</a
          >. We will respond within the timeframe required by law.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority. In the
          Netherlands this is the Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens (autoriteitpersoonsgegevens.nl).
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Cookies -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Cookies and storage</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          Our analytics (Umami) is cookieless &mdash; browsing modpagespeed.com does not set
          tracking cookies. We use strictly necessary browser storage to remember preferences such
          as light or dark mode. If you take out a subscription through our merchant of record, its
          checkout may set its own cookies or browser storage as part of the payment flow, governed
          by its privacy policy.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Changes -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Changes to this notice</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          We may update this notice as our processing changes. The version identifier at the top of
          this page will be updated when we do.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Contact -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          Questions about privacy? Reach us at
          <a
            href="mailto:privacy@we-amp.com"
            class="text-interactive hover:text-interactive-hover underline">privacy@we-amp.com</a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
